{"name":"Taco","hex":"#f3c7b3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Taco","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of TACO; acronym of Trump always chickens out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Taco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Taco","blocks":[{"text":"A taco is a traditional Mexican dish consisting of a small hand-sized corn- or wheat-based tortilla topped with a filling. The tortilla is then folded around the filling and eaten by hand. A taco can be made with a variety of fillings, including beef, pork, chicken, seafood, beans, vegetables, and cheese, and garnished with various condiments, such as salsa, guacamole, or sour cream, and vegetables, such as lettuce, coriander, onion, tomatoes, and chiles. Tacos are a common form of antojitos, or Mexican street food, which have spread around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/001_Tacos_de_carnitas%2C_carne_asada_y_al_pastor.jpg/330px-001_Tacos_de_carnitas%2C_carne_asada_y_al_pastor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taco"},{"title":"Taco (musician)","blocks":[{"text":"Taco Ockerse, also known mononymously as Taco, is an Indonesian-born Dutch musician, actor and entertainer who started his career in Germany. He scored a global hit song in 1982 with a version of \"Puttin' On the Ritz\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Taco_Ockerse_in_Hamburg_%282024%29.jpg/330px-Taco_Ockerse_in_Hamburg_%282024%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taco_(musician)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/01_Tacos_al_Pastor.jpg/500px-01_Tacos_al_Pastor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/01_Tacos_al_Pastor.j